{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b> Fear</b> — stands in place of two." "<b>those who change</b> — from ישנה. The Targum substituted. The meaning: fear HaShem and the king, for HaShem has enthroned the king, to execute justice." "<b>and with those who change</b> — who change in evil deeds, do not mix."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "Reading תרגום החליף ('the Targum substituted') as a statement that Onkelos/Jonathan replaced the Hebrew root with a different Aramaic root; the syntax of the sentence is compressed and the exact referent of החליף is somewhat uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:32.400735078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}